<title>BOTSWANA: TABLE-Sefalana H1 shr falls, div steady.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Sefalana H1 shr falls, div steady.</headline>
<dateline>GABORONE 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr ended April 30</p>
<p>			(million pula unless stated)</p>
<p>    Eps (thebe)		38.8   vs   43.2</p>
<p>    Div (thebe)		15.0   vs   15.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	     6.20  vs    6.91</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		     4.01  vs    5.74</p>
<p>    Tax			   0.14  vs    0.86</p>
<p>    Turnover		   85.20  vs   93.89</p>
<p>Div payable: August 15</p>
<p>On register: August 1</p>
<p>Full name: Sefalana Holding Company Limited</p>
<p>NOTE - The milling firm said the comparatively low demand for maize products had continued during the period. There had still been an abundance of sorghum available from the 1996 bumper harvest.</p>
<p>However, there were signs of an increase in demand for the company's products and it was hoped the next six months would see an increase in production of both maize meal and sorghum milling operations.</p>
<p>-- Gaborone newsroom +267 347182</p>
</text>
